From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:12:25 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: live folders fed by an RSS/Atom feed or a GitHub
 search
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Make Live…" in a pinned folder's menu takes an address in place of its
name: an RSS (2.0/1.0) or Atom feed, or a GitHub search page (fetched
through GitHub's search API). The folder then shows the first 10 items as
pinned rows, refreshed every 30 minutes while a window is open (links kept
by URL keep their ids, so an open tab stays theirs). A small bolt marks
it; "Change Live Address…" and "Stop Live Updates" (the items stay). An
address that gives no items is refused and the folder stays as it was.
No cookies are sent; XML goes through the data decoder. Item.live_url and
SidebarHandler.SetFolderLive appended. Test switches:
--meridian-test-live-folder-seconds, --meridian-test-github-api.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
